---
/**
 * Bay 12, moving from Formspree: what changes, @sendm8/react for React apps, plain fetch, and a prompt for AI assistants.
 */
import CodeBlock from '../../ui/CodeBlock.astro';
import CodeTabs from '../../ui/CodeTabs.astro';
import Callout from '../Callout.astro';
import DocsSection from './DocsSection.astro';
import { limits, site } from '../../../config/site';
import { FORM } from './docsSections';

const htmlBefore = `
<form action="https://formspree.io/f/xyzabcde" method="POST">
  <input name="email" type="email" required>
  <textarea name="message"></textarea>
  <input type="hidden" name="_subject" value="New enquiry">
  <input type="text" name="_gotcha" style="display:none">
  <button>Send</button>
</form>`;

const htmlAfter = `
<form action="${FORM}" method="POST">
  <input name="email" type="email" required>
  <textarea name="message"></textarea>
  <input type="hidden" name="_subject" value="New enquiry">
  <input type="text" name="_gotcha" style="display:none">
  <button>Send</button>
</form>`;

const fetchCode = `
const res = await fetch("${FORM}", {
  method: "POST",
  body: new FormData(form),
  headers: { Accept: "application/json" },
});
const result = await res.json();

if (result.ok) {
  showThanks();
} else {
  // One sentence for the whole form. Field problems are also in
  // result.errors, shaped like Formspree's: [{ field, code, message }].
  showError(result.error.message);
}`;

const reactCode = `
import { useForm, ValidationError } from "@sendm8/react"; // was "@formspree/react"

export function ContactForm() {
  const [state, handleSubmit] = useForm("k3x9q2m7ab"); // was useForm("xyzabcde")

  if (state.succeeded) return <p>Thanks! It's on its way.</p>;

  return (
    <form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
      <input name="email" type="email" required />
      <ValidationError field="email" errors={state.errors} />
      <textarea name="message" required />
      <ValidationError errors={state.errors} />
      <button disabled={state.submitting}>Send</button>
    </form>
  );
}`;

const reactInstall = `
npm uninstall @formspree/react
npm install @sendm8/react`;

const prompt = `
Migrate this app's forms from Formspree to sendm8. Read ${site.url}/llms-full.txt first.

Endpoint mapping (Formspree → sendm8):
- https://formspree.io/f/xyzabcde → ${FORM}

1. Find every Formspree usage: "formspree.io", "@formspree/react", "@formspree/ajax",
   data-fs-* attributes, and environment variables holding Formspree form IDs.
2. HTML forms: change only the action URL. Field names stay the same.
3. JavaScript submissions: POST to the sendm8 URL with "Accept: application/json".
   Success is { ok: true, id }. Failure is { ok: false, error: { code, message }, errors? }:
   error.message is always there. errors (field problems only) matches Formspree's
   [{ field, code, message }], so code reading it per field can stay.
4. Replace @formspree/react with @sendm8/react (same useForm and ValidationError API):
   change the import and the form id. Keep field-level <ValidationError field="..." />, and
   make sure there's also one without a field prop: errors like the monthly limit aren't
   about a field.
   Replace @formspree/ajax with fetch or the sendm8 helper script. Then remove the old packages.
5. Don't change styling, copy or field names.
6. List every file you changed, and anything you couldn't migrate.`;
---

<DocsSection id="formspree" kicker="Bring your forms">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      sendm8 reads the same field names as Formspree, so a plain HTML form moves with a one-line change: the <code>action</code> URL. Code that sends
      forms with JavaScript needs a small change to how it reads errors.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p class="label steps-lead">Moving a form</p>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      <strong>Get a sendm8 endpoint.</strong> Create a form in the <a href="/app">dashboard</a> and copy its URL, or skip signing up and use <code>{site.endpointBase}you@example.com</code>.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Swap the URL</strong> everywhere the form posts to <code>https://formspree.io/f/…</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Send a test submission</strong> and check it arrives where you expect. Then add Discord, Slack, Telegram or webhooks if you like.</li>
  </ol>

  <CodeTabs
    class="wide"
    name="Formspree form before and after"
    tabs={[
      { label: 'After', lang: 'html', filename: 'contact.html', code: htmlAfter, highlight: [1] },
      { label: 'Before', lang: 'html', filename: 'contact.html', code: htmlBefore, highlight: [1] },
    ]}
  />

  <h3 class="ds-h3" id="formspree-mapping">What maps to what</h3>
  <div class="table-wrap wide">
    <table class="table">
      <caption class="sr-only">Formspree features and their sendm8 equivalents</caption>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Formspree</th>
          <th scope="col">sendm8</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>https://formspree.io/f/&lbrace;id&rbrace;</code></td>
          <td><code>{site.endpointBase}&lbrace;id&rbrace;</code>, or <code>{site.endpointBase}&lbrace;your email&rbrace;</code> with no account</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>_replyto</code> or <code>email</code>, <code>_subject</code>, <code>_next</code>, <code>_gotcha</code>, <code>_cc</code></td>
          <td>The same. <code>_next</code> must be on one of the form’s allowed domains, and <code>_cc</code> only copies addresses verified in your account.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Other underscore fields</td>
          <td>Ignored and not stored.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>JSON success: <code>&lbrace; ok: true &rbrace;</code></td>
          <td><code>&lbrace; ok: true, id &rbrace;</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>JSON errors: an <code>errors</code> array</td>
          <td><code>&lbrace; ok: false, error: &lbrace; code, message &rbrace; &rbrace;</code> with a matching HTTP status, plus the same <code>errors</code> array when a field is at fault. <a href="/docs/ajax/">AJAX / fetch</a>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>@formspree/react</code> (<code>useForm</code>, <code>ValidationError</code>)</td>
          <td><a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@sendm8/react"><code>@sendm8/react</code></a>, with the same API. Change the import and the form id.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>@formspree/ajax</code> and <code>data-fs-*</code> attributes</td>
          <td>The helper script and <code>data-sendm8</code> attributes. <a href="/docs/ajax-helper/">AJAX without writing JavaScript</a>.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3 class="ds-h3" id="formspree-code">React and JavaScript</h3>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      In a React app, swap <code>@formspree/react</code> for <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@sendm8/react"><code>@sendm8/react</code></a>. It has the same
      <code>useForm</code> and <code>ValidationError</code>, so the import and the form id are the only changes. Field errors work the same, and every failure also comes with
      one error for the whole form (some, like the monthly limit, aren’t about a field), so keep a <code>&lt;ValidationError&gt;</code> without
      a <code>field</code> somewhere in the form too.
    </p>
  </div>
  <CodeTabs
    class="wide"
    name="Migrating JavaScript submissions"
    tabs={[
      { label: 'React', lang: 'jsx', filename: 'ContactForm.jsx', code: reactCode, highlight: [1, 4, 11, 13] },
      { label: 'Install', lang: 'sh', filename: 'terminal', code: reactInstall },
      { label: 'fetch', lang: 'js', filename: 'contact.js', code: fetchCode, highlight: [13] },
    ]}
  />

  <h3 class="ds-h3" id="formspree-ai">Migrating with an AI assistant</h3>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      These docs are also published as Markdown for AI assistants: <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a> lists every section, and <a href="/llms-full.txt">/llms-full.txt</a> has all of them in one file. Create your sendm8 forms first (an assistant can’t do that for you), then
      give it a prompt like this in the app you’re migrating.
    </p>
  </div>
  <CodeBlock code={prompt} lang="text" filename="prompt.txt" class="wide" />

  <Callout title="Worth knowing" kind="info">
    <p>
      Uploads are capped at {limits.fileUploadMb} MB a file. If your Formspree forms only accept submissions from certain sites, add those domains under <strong>Form settings → General → Allowed domains</strong>.
    </p>
  </Callout>
</DocsSection>

<style>
  .wide {
    max-width: 100%;
  }
</style>
